###Pure
// Multi-file repro for the compile-pure association-property propagation
// bug. The deep-property keys `parent.children` / `parent.name` in the
// copy expression `^$d(parent.children=[], …)` need the `parent` property
// to be resolvable on Department — which it is only after the
// SubOrganization Association's pass 2 attaches `parent` / `children`
// to Organization. Because compileFiles processes files in declared
// order and this function file precedes `model.pure` below, the
// function's pass 2 runs BEFORE the association's pass 2. Java's
// bootstrap compiler tolerates this; compile-pure does not yet — so
// this test passes on bootstrap and witnesses the bug on Truffle.
function test::a::useInheritedAssoc(d:test::a::Department[1]):test::a::Department[1]
{
  ^$d(parent.children=[], parent.name='TechParent1');
}

###File model.pure
Class test::a::Organization
{
  name : String[1];
}

Association test::a::SubOrganization
{
  parent : test::a::Organization[0..1];
  children : test::a::Organization[*];
}

Class test::a::Department extends test::a::Organization
{
}

